@import('./LegalDocument')

<!-- Privacy content rendered inside the shared dashboard legal shell. -->
<template>
  <LegalDocument
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    summary="This notice explains how the Stacks dashboard handles information used to operate your application."
  >
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">Information handled</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
        The dashboard processes account details, session security data, audit information, and the application records needed for the pages and actions you use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">Local project access</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
        In development, the dashboard reads your local project configuration, database, and framework state. It does not invent provider activity or send project data to an external service unless you invoke a feature that requires that provider.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">Credentials and providers</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
        Secrets remain in server-side configuration and must not be rendered into dashboard pages. When you use a connected provider, that provider processes requests under its own terms and privacy policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-lg text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">Retention and requests</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
        Retention follows your application configuration and the policies of connected storage providers. Contact your application administrator to request access, correction, export, or deletion of personal information.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalDocument>
</template>
